{"base_rate":0.022696929238985315,"brier":0.028587182910547397,"bss":-0.2887687399549983,"bss_hi":-0.08963429965630448,"bss_lo":-1.0074682598591143,"country":"MX","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.03108144192256342,"ess":423.41755888650704,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Mexicali</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Mexicali rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 2 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (25%), believe about\n<b>6%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 749 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nEL CENTRO 2 SSW, 18.6 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.29, ranked 108 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(107&ndash;109) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>567</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>105</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">2 of 3 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Mexicali</b> <span class=\"muted\">MX</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">2 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>-0.29</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>107&ndash;109\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>749 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Mexicali &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Mexicali\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 67.44,361.2 145.71844155844155,259.0909090909091 145.71844155844155,320.54545454545456 67.44,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"373.7383177570093\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"373.7383177570093\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,376.22222222222223 67.44,371.6 145.71844155844155,358.3636363636364\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 567 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"376.22222222222223\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 3%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 105 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"67.44\" cy=\"371.6\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 25%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"145.71844155844155\" cy=\"358.3636363636364\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(2%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Mexicali the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (-0.07) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-1.67).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>176</td><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'>-1.674</td><td class='num'>5.4%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>2%</td><td class='num'>-0.221</td><td class='num'>0.3%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>177</td><td class='num'>6%</td><td class='num'>-0.102</td><td class='num'>4.5%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>217</td><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'>-0.072</td><td class='num'>0.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":32.62781,"lon":-115.45446,"n":749,"n_cities":109,"name":"Mexicali","offset_days":2,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":567,"obs":0.015873015873015872,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.02666666666666667,"n":105,"obs":0.02857142857142857,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.2477922077922078,"n":77,"obs":0.06493506493506493,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":18.6,"rank":108,"rank_hi":109.0,"rank_lo":107.0,"reliability":0.0036286604361370728,"resolution":0.00022349660371695975,"slug":"mexicali","station":"EL CENTRO 2 SSW","timezone":"America/Tijuana"}